    "policy": "Every Prisma model declares HOW it is isolated. Strategies: direct-company (companyId column \u2014 the company condition composes directly); employee-child-relation (Prisma Employee relation \u2014 company scope composes through scopedEmployeeRelationWhere's JOIN, no materialized id lists); vendor-plane (vendorId only \u2014 isolation by query-time composition; every read/write path must carry its scope through employeeScopeFilter/scopedEmployeeWhere or a parent linkage); saas-plane (no vendorId \u2014 platform tables outside the tenant plane). scripts/check-model-isolation.mjs ENFORCES this registry in CI: a model missing from the registry fails the gate, a registry entry without its model fails the gate, and a declared strategy that does not match the schema's structure fails the gate. The materialized employee-child strategy is FORBIDDEN since FIN-017 (performance: id-list IN-clauses at 5k-50k employees).",
